<section id="about" class="section about">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h-section">About</h2>
    </header>

    <div class="about__prose">
      <p>
        Give me the hard, ambiguous product. I'll take it from the user problem through the system
        that runs it in production. At the NBA that meant the live score strip, built from its
        first commit, and the path from sign-in to game access. At Bar Savvy it means everything,
        since I'm often the only engineer. I've done that alongside my work at LV Collective, where
        I now spend as much time teaching AI as I do building.
      </p>
      <p>
        I build this way because it lets a small team move like a much larger one, without the mess
        that usually comes with moving fast. It's why the people I hand this to start shipping work
        they couldn't before. The harness is what makes the speed safe enough to trust.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

